# SSSF environment. Copy to .env at the target repo root and fill in.
#
# THE STARTER ROSTER NEEDS NOTHING IN THIS FILE.
# It ships two subscription-billed interfaces and no API keys: four agents on
# `coding_agent: claude_code` (your Claude Pro/Max plan) and the reviewer on
# `coding_agent: codex` (your ChatGPT plan). Authenticate once each, outside
# this file — miss either and validate() fails before anything spawns:
#
#     claude login          # or: claude setup-token   (headless box)
#     codex login           # or: codex login --with-api-key
#
# You need a key here only when you add a `coding_agent: pi` agent — see the
# commented `challenger` example at the bottom of sssf.config.yaml.
#
# WHICH KEY DEPENDS ON THE PROVIDER YOU NAME. A pi `model:` is written as
# provider/model-id; the provider half decides the key, and which key pi reads
# for that provider comes from ~/.pi/agent/models.json. The three below are the
# common ones, left blank on purpose — fill in only what your roster names.
#
# Nothing validates this for you. `agents.validate()` checks that a pi model
# resolves in the catalog, not that its provider is reachable or that its key is
# set, so a missing key shows up when that agent runs, not at startup.

OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
FIREWORKS_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# CLAUDE CODE AGENTS (coding_agent: claude_code) NEED NO KEY HERE.
# They run on your Claude Pro/Max subscription. Authenticate once, outside this
# file: `claude login`, or `claude setup-token` on a headless box.
#
# Do NOT add ANTHROPIC_API_KEY expecting it to be used — it would be, and that
# is the problem. Claude Code prefers an API key over the subscription, so
# agent_cc.ts strips ANTHROPIC_API_KEY / ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN /
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL / the Bedrock and Vertex switches from the child
# environment. Bun loads this file into every ADW and every child process, so
# without that scrub a key set here for a *pi* agent's provider would silently
# move your Claude Code agents onto metered API billing. The scrub is per-child:
# pi agents still see the key normally.
#
# Subscription agents report cost 0.00, because nothing was billed per token.
# The CLI's own API-price estimate is suppressed rather than mixed into a run
# total alongside real spend; set SSSF_CC_USE_API_KEY=1 and it reports in full.
# Tokens are the signal for subscription work, and they are always exact.

# Optional overrides
# PI_PATH=pi                       # pi binary if not on PATH
# PI_MODELS_PATH=~/.pi/agent/models.json
# ENGINEER_NAME=                   # engineer lane label, defaults to git user.name
# CLAUDE_CODE_PATH=claude          # claude binary if not on PATH
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=         # `claude setup-token` output; survives the scrub
# SSSF_CC_USE_API_KEY=1            # skip the scrub — spend an API key (or a proxy) on purpose
# SSSF_CC_SETTING_SOURCES=project,local   # add `user` to let your ~/.claude settings/hooks into runs

# SANDBOX DISPATCH (just sandbox-sdlc — cookbooks/sandbox.md)
# CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN above is REQUIRED with remote.claude_auth: subscription
# (the default): it is the credential the dispatch ships to the VM so in-VM
# claude_code agents bill your Claude plan. It is revocable — treat it that way.
# Codex needs no key here: the default (remote.codex_auth: gateway) runs it
# keylessly against exe.dev's LLM gateway. Never share ~/.codex/auth.json with
# a VM — OpenAI's refresh-token rotation corrupts the losing copy.
#
# GH_TOKEN=                        # only with remote.clone_via: token — a fine-grained
#                                  # PAT scoped to ONE repo, Contents: Read. The default
#                                  # clone_via: integration needs no token at all.
